FIRST_CHUNK SWEEP -- how big should the first tail read be?

Window: the newest 40 turns, over 10 real transcripts. The answer is identical
for every candidate (flags.py's own self-test asserts first_chunk cannot change
the result, only the cost) -- so this table is purely about cost.

 first_chunk     total MB   reads        files that grew
--------------------------------------------------------
         64K        12.98      30           10 of 10  
        128K        12.09      23           10 of 10  
        256K        12.41      20           10 of 10  
        512K        10.94      13            3 of 10  
       1024K         9.97      10            0 of 10    <- current default  <- cheapest here
       2048K        19.88      10            0 of 10  
       4096K        35.32      10            0 of 10  

The current default is the cheapest candidate over this corpus.

A LIMIT WORTH STATING: this is one corpus, and the optimum is a property of how
many bytes a turn takes in it. A deployment whose turns are much smaller or much
larger should re-run this rather than inherit the number -- which is why
read_window() takes first_chunk as a parameter at all.
